    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d535">

                <pb facs="0725" n="611" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg611"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.51/1377: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-01-30T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 30,
                                1922—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>4. Deliver following to President King—“I thank you for your message received
                    January 26th<anchor n="7" xml:id="d535-f1"/> informing me that loan agreement
                    has been approved by Liberian legislature without amendment.<anchor n="8"
                        xml:id="d535-f2"/> The matter is pending in Congress and I trust that
                    favorable action will soon be taken.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d535-f1" n="7" xml:id="d535-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d535-f2" n="8" xml:id="d535-f2-content">
                <p>The agreement was approved Jan. 23.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
